[2026-06-07T02:01:44.772Z] [INFO] {"body":"## Summary\n- Add recursive semantic facet/root seed coverage for issue 398, including Links-root ontology data, requirements and vision updates, and the case-study research artifacts under docs/case-studies/issue-398.\n- Migrate meaning seed data away from quoted prose fields into id-first LiNo facts using surfaces, source ids, and generated compatibility text only at read time.\n- Move lossless Wikidata snapshots into data/cache/wikidata as one .lino file per required entity or lexeme, remove the legacy data/seed/api-cache bundle, and add rerunnable Rust migration/conversion scripts.\n- Update parser, worker fallback seed loading, translation seed bridge, and data audits so the app reads the migrated format consistently.\n- Keep the CI file-size gate focused on editable Rust/LiNo files while excluding generated Wikidata source-cache snapshots that must remain one file per entity.\n\n## Verification\n- quote grep over data/seed and data/cache returned no matches\n- old-field grep for gloss, description, meaning, and word seed records returned no matches\n- rustc scripts/migrate-meaning-seed.rs -o /tmp/migrate-meaning-seed && /tmp/migrate-meaning-seed\n- node --check src/web/formal_ai_worker.js && node --check src/web/seed_loader.js\n- cargo test --test unit data_files -- --nocapture\n- cargo test\n- cargo clippy --all-targets --all-features\n- cargo fmt --all -- --check\n- rust-script scripts/check-file-size.rs\n- rust-script --test scripts/check-file-size.rs\n\nNo screenshot attached because this change is semantic seed/parser/cache behavior, not visual UI work.","headRefOid":"5b8f814dd643b1540d8d51204cac6faead1c006c","isDraft":false,"title":"Add recursive semantic facets and id-based LiNo seed","url":"https://github.com/link-assistant/formal-ai/pull/399"}
