[2026-06-07T02:06:20.967Z] [INFO] {"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1094","type":"reasoning","text":"**Examining session status**\n\nI'm checking on the status of the e2e upload and the session. It seems like the upload is in progress, but I'm not sure if the watch session is still running. It looks like I can't close it right now, and ‘gh run view’ indicates that it might not have terminated.\n\nMaybe I should check if any exec sessions are running. I'll consider using commands to identify and potentially stop them without causing issues, but I need to be careful about that.\n**Considering process termination**\n\nI'm thinking about how we started this process and whether I can terminate it with `pkill`. It seems like this might be okay since it wouldn't be destructive to the repository. I’m considering using the command `pkill -f \"gh run watch 27079832872\"`. \n\nI can also check for other instances with `pgrep -af \"gh run watch\"` to see what's running. I just need to be cautious and ensure that I'm not disrupting anything important."}}
