[2026-06-07T02:06:50.228Z] [INFO] {"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1105","type":"reasoning","text":"**Considering command execution**\n\nI'm thinking about using `sleep` to create a delay for executing a command. I could run the `gh` command after a 30-second pause using `sleep 30`, but since it uses shell time, I’m trying to ensure it doesn’t output anything annoying. Maybe using `exec \"sleep 30\"` could work, allowing me to query afterward. I want to make sure there’s no chaining issue, so a separate sleep followed by the query might be best."}}
