m/link-assistant/formal-ai/pull/399#issuecomment-4640365064","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/formal-ai/issues/399","id":4640365064,"node_id":"IC_kwDOSbOoU88AAAABFJZaCA","user":{"login":"konard","id":1431904,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzE5MDQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1431904?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard","html_url":"https://github.com/konard","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-06-06T21:08:27Z","updated_at":"2026-06-06T21:08:27Z","body":"## ✅ Ready to merge\n\nThis pull request is now ready to be merged:\n- All CI checks have passed\n- No merge conflicts\n- No pending changes\n\n---\n*Monitored by hive-mind with --auto-restart-until-mergeable flag*","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/formal-ai/issues/comments/4640365064/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/formal-ai/issues/comments/4640715931","html_url":"https://github.com/link-assistant/formal-ai/pull/399#issuecomment-4640715931","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/formal-ai/issues/399","id":4640715931,"node_id":"IC_kwDOSbOoU88AAAABFJu0mw","user":{"login":"konard","id":1431904,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzE5MDQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1431904?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard","html_url":"https://github.com/konard","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-06-06T23:03:09Z","updated_at":"2026-06-06T23:03:09Z","body":"## Draft: a self-defining semantic root in Links Notation\n\nFollowing the thread on #398 that the meaning data structure is \"fake\" and still leans on hardcoded English, here is a **draft** of a core semantic structure built strictly on [Links Theory](https://github.com/link-foundation/meta-theory): everything is a link, every word is a reference, and the irreducible primitives are defined by their **own structural self-equation** (self-reference with meaningful structure) rather than by English synonyms.\n\nBecause everything is already a link, definitions never say \"link\" just to say it — a reference is named only when it adds real structure.\n\n### Rules for constructing the semantic network\n\n1. **Global, reusable references.** Every reference is defined once, globally, and reused to define others. The network is one shared namespace; a definition anywhere is usable everywhere.\n2. **One symbol, one meaning.** A reference has exactly one meaning. If the same symbol is found with two meanings, **split it into two symbols** (`bank-river` vs `bank-money`, `is-identity` vs `is-a-kind-of`). No token is ambiguous for human or machine.\n3. **Natural-language, human-readable references**, in a **simple, easily-parsable subset of English**: lowercase words, hyphens to bind a multi-word reference into one symbol (`any-of-reference`, `is-a-kind-of`), the colon for \"is a\", and a small set of **defined** connectives (`of`, `from`, `to`, `and`) — each itself a link in the network, never undefined prose.\n4. **Define a relation by the two links it connects and cannot exist without**, plus its direction. Ask: *which two links does this connect, and could it exist without them?* Example: `child` is the offspring **of** `father` **and** `mother`; remove either parent and `child` has nothing to be. That dependency is the definition.\n5. **If no constitutive relation exists, define by supertype** with `is-a-kind-of`. This is the fallback for a category rather than a connection.\n6. **`type` is its own type** — `type: type type` — self-defined, with specifics layered on afterward.\n7. **Core links are fixed** (`reference`, `link`, `type`); everything else must be compatible with them.\n\n```lino\n# root: self-witnessing primitives, each line is what it defines\nreference: reference-action link\nlink: link-action any-of-reference\ntype: type type\n\n# action and quantity forms; repeatable-from-zero means n in N0\nreference-action: makes reference point-at link\nlink-action: makes link from any-of-reference\nany-of-reference: reference repeatable-from-zero\nany-of-link: link repeatable-from-zero\nrepeatable-from-zero: same link-action zero-or-more\nmakes: link-action that brings into being\npoint-at: reference-action toward link\n\n# defined connectives, so bodies never use undefined prose\nof: belonging from part to whole\nfrom: source end of direction\nto: target end of direction\nand: this together-with that\n\n# structural primitives, defined by self-equation\nnot: not (not not)\nis-identity: same applied-to same\nsame: not (not same)\nother: not same\nsingle: not other\nor-else: choice between this and other\nzero: count of empty\none: count of single\nmore: one and one\n\n# the three specific senses of english is; bare is is never used\nis-a-kind-of: subtype toward supertype\nis-property: property held-by subject\nheld-by: from property to subject\n\n# quantity: amount and size kept distinct\nquantity: amount or-else size\namount: count of any-of-link\nsize: extent of single link\ncount: how-many over distinct reference\nextent: how-much over single reference\ndistinct: other and other\nany: quantity not fixed\nfixed: same over repeatable-from-zero\n```\n\n### More concepts, built on the root above\n\nStill pure links, still no opaque English payload — scaling to structure, number, logic, sets, change, formal and natural language.\n\n```lino\n# structure and identity\nsequence: order over any-of-reference\norder: direction over reference\nfirst: not after-another\nlast: not before-another\nbefore-another: other toward first\nafter-another: other toward last\nempty: any-of-reference of-size zero\nof-size: from any-of-reference to size\npart: belonging from smaller to whole\nwhole: has-part any-of-part\nhas-part: from whole to part\nany-of-part: part repeatable-from-zero\nholon: part and whole together\nnesting: part within part\nposition: place of reference over order\n\n# typing and ontology\nsubtype: is-a-kind-of toward supertype\nsupertype: has subtype\ninstance: is-a-kind-of toward type\ncategory: type over any-of-instance\nany-of-instance: instance repeatable-from-zero\nroot-type: type not is-a-kind-of other\ndefined-by: from concept to any-of-concept\nabstract: concept not held-by instance\nconcrete: concept held-by instance\n\n# number, from the meta-theory N0\nnumber: type of count\nsuccessor: from number to one-more number\npredecessor: from number to one-less number\none-more: more by one\none-less: less by one\nless: not more\nsum: from number and number to number\ndifference: from number and number to less number\nproduct: sum repeated by number\nnatural-number: from zero by successor\ndigit: character denotes number\n\n# logic, toward many-valued truth\nand-both: this and that hold\nor: not (not this and not that)\nimplies: not (this and not that)\ntrue: holds-for any\nfalse: not true\nunknown: not true and not false\nholds-for: from truth-value to proposition\nproposition: meaning has truth-value\ntruth-value: quantity over proposition\ncontradiction: proposition true and false\n\n# set and relation, as ordered-unique sequences per the paper\nset: sequence of distinct ordered reference\nmember: belonging from reference to set\nsubset: set of member of set\nunion: from set and set to set\nintersection: from set and set to common member\nrelation: from link to link\ndirection: order from source to target\nsource: first of relation\ntarget: last of relation\nfunction: relation from one to one\n\n# time and change, since the network is mutable\ntime: order over change\nchange: link-action makes link other\nbefore: less over time\nafter: more over time\nstate: link at single time\nversion: state of link at change\nmutation: change over substitution\nsubstitution: link-action replaces pattern by pattern\npattern: matches any-of-link\nmatches: from pattern to same-shape link\n\n# language layer: words attach to meaning without privileging any tongue\nlanguage: from meaning to any-of-expression\nany-of-expression: expression repeatable-from-zero\nexpression: order of any-of-character for meaning\ncharacter: is-a-kind-of toward form\nform: held-by perceivable\nperceivable: property sensed\nword: expression stands-for single meaning\nstands-for: from expression to meaning\nphrase: expression from word and word\ndenotes: from expression to meaning\nconnotes: from expression to other meaning\ntranslation: from expression to other-expression of same meaning\nsynonym: expression denotes same meaning\nhomonym: expression denotes other meaning\nsense: single meaning of expression\nlexeme: word of any-of-sense\n\n# grammar of natural language, all as links\npart-of-speech: type of word\nnoun: part-of-speech denotes entity\nverb: part-of-speech denotes act\nentity: concept held-by bounded\nact: link-action change makes\nsubject: source of verb\nobject: target of verb\nmodifier: from word to narrowed meaning\nnarrowed: smaller meaning toward specific\n\n# formal and programming languages, parsed into the same network\ngrammar: from language to any-of-rule\nany-of-rule: rule repeatable-from-zero\nrule: pattern matches expression of language\ntoken: smallest expression\nnode: part of parse-tree\nparse-tree: order of node by rule\ncst: parse-tree of any-of-character\nast: parse-tree without trivia\ntrivia: character not held-by meaningful\nmixed-language: expression from expression of other language\nregion: part of expression in single language\n\n# source and provenance, the #398 grounding requirement\nsource-of-truth: grounds any-of-link\ngrounds: from source to grounded link\nexternal-source: source not within network\noverride: replaces link by marked link\nmarked: held-by explicit\ncached: stores source-response for compare\ncompare: from link to link by same\n\n# formality, toward relative-meta-logic\nformality: quantity from informal to formal\nformal: meaning fully defined-by relation\ninformal: meaning not fully defined-by relation\nvariable: meaning not fixed\nrange: any from least to most\nclarify: change from informal to more formal\n```\n\n### Worked example: applying the construction rules\n\n```lino\n# rule 5: not relations between two links, so defined by supertype\nperson: animal able-to reason\nparent: person has-child child\nmother: parent held-by female\nfather: parent held-by male\n\n# rule 4: each relation defined by the two links it connects, with direction\nchild: offspring of father and mother\nhas-child: from parent to child\nmotherhood: from mother to child\nfatherhood: from father to child\nsibling: from child to other child of same parents\nspouse: from person to married person\n\n# rule 2: split an ambiguous symbol into distinct senses\nbank-river: land beside water\nbank-money: organization keeps money\n# never a single bank\n```\n\n`child` cannot exist without `father` and `mother` — that pair, as the offspring relation, is its whole definition. `mother` is not a connection between two links, so it falls back to its supertype `parent` plus the specific `held-by female`. And `bank` is split, because one symbol carries only one meaning.\n\n### Status of this draft\n\n- **An example of the core structure, not a finished spec.** A draft, and can be done better.\n- It **closes** (every token used reduces to defined ones) but does not claim non-circular grounding: the bottom is a small set of mutually-defining cycles (`count`/`how-many` content, the `not`/`same` self-equations, and `reference`/`link` themselves). The meta-theory explicitly permits self-reference and cycles — this is the intended bottom, the point/line primitives of the system.\n- Strongest parts: the **self-equations** (`not: not (not not)`) and the **one-symbol-one-meaning** sense-splitting. The connectives (`of`, `from`, `to`, `and`) are kept but **defined as links**, so bodies never use undefined prose.\n\n### Where this should go next\n\nThis can and should be made **even better, and fully proven formally**, with [relative-meta-logic](https://github.com/link-foundation/relative-meta-logic): each definition link becomes a proposition with a truth/typing judgment, the self-equations get checked as genuine fixed points, the ontology roots get dependent types (`(Type: Type Type)`), and the whole semantic root is verified for consistency rather than asserted — a **solid semantic foundation that fully takes advantage of Links Meta Theory**.\n\nGoal: replace the English-keyed `gloss`/`description` seed with this links-network root, so meanings, senses, concepts, and types are recorded as links that define themselves — and translations to any language fall out as `denotes` / `translation` links rather than hardcoded pairs.\n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/formal-ai/issues/comments/4640715931/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/formal-ai/issues/comments/4640770087","html_url":"https://github.com/link-assistant/formal-ai/pull/399#issuecomment-4640770087","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/formal-ai/issues/399","id":4640770087,"node_id":"IC_kwDOSbOoU88AAAABFJyIJw","user":{"login":"konard","id":1431904,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzE5MDQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1431904?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard","html_url":"https://github.com/konard","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-06-06T23:23:45Z","updated_at":"2026-06-06T23:23:45Z","body":"🤖 **AI Work Session Started**\n\nStarting automated work session at 2026-06-06T23:23:43.528Z\n\nThe PR has been converted to draft mode while work is in progress.\n\n_This comment marks the beginning of an AI work session. Please wait for the session to finish, and provide your feedback._","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/formal-ai/issues/comments/4640770087/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/formal-ai/issues/comments/4640820263","html_url":"https://github.com/link-assistant/formal-ai/pull/399#issuecomment-4640820263","issue_url":"https://ap
