[2026-06-07T02:08:41.965Z] [STDOUT] ormal-ai/issues/399","id":4640820263,"node_id":"IC_kwDOSbOoU88AAAABFJ1MJw","user":{"login":"konard","id":1431904,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzE5MDQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1431904?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard","html_url":"https://github.com/konard","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-06-06T23:50:43Z","updated_at":"2026-06-06T23:50:43Z","body":"<!-- hive-mind:working-session-summary -->\n## Working session summary\n\nFinished PR #399: https://github.com/link-assistant/formal-ai/pull/399\n\nImplemented and pushed commit `f1db0382` on `issue-398-b349f91c312f`. The PR is no longer draft and now has the title `Add recursive semantic facets and Links root seed`.\n\nWhat changed:\n- Added the Links Theory semantic root seed with recursive root terms, explicit self-equation facets, defined connectives, split `is` senses, quantity roots, and one-symbol-one-meaning `bank_river` / `bank_money`.\n- Wired the new seed into embedded seed loading.\n- Added focused tests covering root reachability, self-equations, connectives, `is` senses, and ambiguous symbol splitting.\n- Updated requirements, vision docs, changelog, and issue case-study docs.\n\nValidation:\n- Local full checks passed, including `cargo fmt`, clippy with `-Dwarnings`, full Rust tests, doc tests, seed sync check, web bundle checks, e2e support checks, changelog/version checks.\n- Fresh GitHub CI for latest SHA `f1d**********************************997` passed: https://github.com/link-assistant/formal-ai/actions/runs/27077141619\n- Working tree is clean on `issue-398-b349f91c312f`.\n\nOnly remaining CI annotations are warning-only existing file-size warnings and a GitHub Actions Node 20 deprecation notice.\n\n---\n*This summary was automatically extracted from the AI working session output.*","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/formal-ai/issues/comments/4640820263/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/formal-ai/issues/comments/4640820948","html_url":"https://github.com/link-assistant/formal-ai/pull/399#issuecomment-4640820948","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/formal-ai/issues/399","id":4640820948,"node_id":"IC_kwDOSbOoU88AAAABFJ1O1A","user":{"login":"konard","id":1431904,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzE5MDQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1431904?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard","html_url":"https://github.com/konard","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-06-06T23:50:54Z","updated_at":"2026-06-06T23:50:54Z","body":"## 🤖 Solution Draft Log\nThis log file contains the complete execution trace of the AI solution draft process.\n\n### 💰 **Cost estimation:**\n- Model: GPT-5.5\n- Provider: OpenAI\n- Public pricing estimate: $12.232846\n\n### 📊 **Context and tokens usage:**\n- 391.3K / 1.1M (37%) input tokens, 46.5K / 128K (36%) output tokens\n\nTotal: (391.3K + 6.2M cached) input tokens, 46.5K output tokens, $12.232846 cost\n\n### 🤖 **Models used:**\n- Tool: OpenAI Codex\n- Requested: `gpt-5.5`\n- **Model: GPT-5.5** (`gpt-5.5`)\n\n### 📎 **Log file uploaded as Repository** (67136KB)\n- [View complete solution draft log](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/konard/public-logs/main/log-tmp-solution-draft-log-pr-1780789847402.txt/tmp-solution-draft-log-pr-1780789847402.txt)\n\n---\n*Now working session is ended, feel free to review and add any feedback on the solution draft.*","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/formal-ai/issues/comments/4640820948/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/formal-ai/issues/comments/4640828224","html_url":"https://github.com/link-assistant/formal-ai/pull/399#issuecomment-4640828224","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/formal-ai/issues/399","id":4640828224,"node_id":"IC_kwDOSbOoU88AAAABFJ1rQA","user":{"login":"konard","id":1431904,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzE5MDQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1431904?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard","html_url":"https://github.com/konard","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-06-06T23:53:15Z","updated_at":"2026-06-06T23:53:15Z","body":"## ✅ Ready to merge\n\nThis pull request is now ready to be merged:\n- All CI checks have passed\n- No merge conflicts\n- No pending changes\n\n---\n*Monitored by hive-mind with --auto-restart-until-mergeable flag*","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/formal-ai/issues/comments/4640828224/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/formal-ai/issues/comments/4640905488","html_url":"https://github.com/link-assistant/formal-ai/pull/399#issuecomment-4640905488","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/formal-ai/issues/399","id":4640905488,"node_id":"IC_kwDOSbOoU88AAAABFJ6ZEA","user":{"login":"konard","id":1431904,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzE5MDQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1431904?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard","html_url":"https://github.com/konard","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-06-07T00:31:25Z","updated_at":"2026-06-07T00:31:25Z","body":"This went in the wrong direction. Read this fully and follow it exactly — do not reinterpret, do not \"improve\" on it, do not add a parallel layer. Where I give real ids below, use those exact ids; do not invent ids or examples.\n\n## The stakes\n\nThe cognition of this formal AI depends directly on how well-structured this data is. A solid, fully-formal semantic foundation is not optional — if it is not done, the system is doomed from the start. There is no way around it. This is a large project; that is fine. It is the foundation everything else stands on.\n\n## What I asked for vs. what happened\n\n**Wanted:** redesign all meanings into the format in [the draft comment](https://github.com/link-assistant/formal-ai/pull/399#issuecomment-4640715931), **algorithmically** (a migration script), not hand-written.\n\n**You did in `f1db0382`:** created a new `data/seed/meanings-links-root.lino` that wraps our template *back inside the exact fake structure we are removing*, and left the old meanings untouched. Top of your file:\n\n```lino\nmeaning \"reference\"\n  gloss \"a link-native pointer ...\"\n  defined_by \"reference_action\"\n  lexeme \"en\"\n    word \"reference\"\n      description \"English noun for a pointer ...\"\n```\n\nThis still has: English-string identity, English free-text `gloss`, English `description`, `defined_by` lists, the redundant `meaning` keyword — and `meanings-semantic-meta.lino` still has 104 old `gloss`/`lexeme`/`description` blocks. This is doubling down on the fake solution.\n\n## Principles you must internalize\n\n1. **Drop the `meaning` keyword.** It serves nothing — everything here is a meaning/link already. Record facts about a defined link by **indentation under that link's id**.\n2. **NO quoted free-text anywhere. A quoted string like `\"relationship or relation\"` is a single opaque reference — that is exactly the fake we are removing.** `gloss \"...\"`, `description \"...\"`, `word \"...\"` are all forbidden: the `\"...\"` is one un-formalized blob, not actual link-references. Text must be **decomposed into real link-references**: a phrase is an ordered link of **word-lexeme ids**; a word surface is an ordered link of **character references** (by Unicode code point). If text cannot yet be resolved to ids, it is stored as explicitly-marked *unformalized-raw* and a test flags it — it is never a quoted reference pretending to be data.\n3. **A description is not data — it is output.** Every human-readable description, in any language, must be **produced by translating the formal definition** into that language. Never store it. If it can be regenerated → don't store it. If it cannot → the meaning is not formalized; fix the formalization.\n4. **\"word\" is not specific enough — and nothing real is defined by itself.** A surface in a real language is never just a word. It is a **lexeme** with a **part of speech** (noun/verb/adjective…), specific **forms** (singular/plural/tense…), each form carrying **grammatical features**, and **senses**. Model lexeme + POS + form + grammatical-feature + sense, all as **real ids**, never a bare word.\n5. **References to sources must be real ids, not words.** Link to `Q121769`, `L5785`, `Q1084` — actual entities — never to a word. A by-word reference is fake.\n6. **Every id line carries a human-readable comment**, so the file is readable without leaving it. The comment is a `#` comment (not data, never a quoted reference); the data stays id-based.\n7. **All examples must be grounded in real fetched data.** Fetch the real ids first. Do not fabricate ids or structure — fabricated examples are how this keeps getting faked.\n\n## Real data to use (verified — use these exact ids)\n\nConcept and lexemes for \"reference\" (fetched from Wikidata just now):\n\n- `Q121769` — concept \"reference\" — *\"relationship between objects in which one object designates ... another object\"*\n- `L5785` — English **noun** lexeme \"reference\"; lexicalCategory `Q1084` (noun); language `Q1860` (English)\n- `L41576` — English **verb** lexeme \"reference\" (same spelling, different lexeme — proof \"word\" is insufficient)\n- `L5785-F1` form \"reference\", grammaticalFeatures `Q110786` (singular)\n- `L5785-F2` form \"references\", grammaticalFeatures `Q146786` (plural)\n- `L5785-S1`…`S4` senses; `L5785-S4` *is* the `Q121769` definition\n- `L166084`, `L166085` — Russian noun lexemes \"ссылка\"\n- `Q1084` = noun, `Q24905` = verb, `Q1860` = English, `Q110786` = singular, `Q146786` = plural\n\n## Precached source data as lino (lossless true conversion)\n\nWe must ship **prefetched/precached `.lino` files** that are the **lossless** representation of the JSON API responses from Wikidata/Wiktionary/Wikipedia — so the system starts fast without hammering APIs, and every `Q…`/`L…` we reference has a real definition available locally, inspectable and updatable.\n\nRules:\n- **Lossless:** every field of the API JSON must be representable in the lino — no data dropped. A round-trip (json → lino → json) must reproduce the original.\n- **True conversion, NOT quoted JSON.** Do not store the JSON string. Convert each JSON object/array/field into links. A JSON object becomes a link whose children are key→value links; arrays become ordered links; scalars become value links.\n- Store under e.g. `data/cache/wikidata/L5785.lino`, one file per entity.\n\n### Worked example — REAL JSON → lino (lossless)\n\nThis is the actual (trimmed) JSON of `L5785`:\n\n```json\n{ \"id\": \"L5785\", \"lexicalCategory\": \"Q1084\", \"language\": \"Q1860\",\n  \"lemmas\": { \"en\": { \"language\": \"en\", \"value\": \"reference\" } },\n  \"forms\": [ { \"id\": \"L5785-F1\",\n      \"representations\": { \"en\": { \"language\": \"en\", \"value\": \"reference\" } },\n      \"grammaticalFeatures\": [ \"Q110786\" ] } ],\n  \"senses\": [ { \"id\": \"L5785-S1\",\n      \"glosses\": { \"en\": { \"language\": \"en\", \"value\": \"relationship or relation (to something)\" } } } ] }\n```\n\nConverted to lino with **zero quoted strings** — every text value decomposed into real link-references. A word-surface is an ordered link of **character references** (Unicode code points); a gloss is an ordered link of **word-lexeme ids**. Comments (`#`) carry the human reading:\n\n```lino\nL5785                              # wikidata lexeme, english noun \"reference\"\n  lexical-category Q1084           # noun\n  language Q1860                   # english\n  lemma en surface-reference       # the lemma's surface, defined below by characters\n  form L5785-F1                    # singular form\n    representation en surface-reference\n    grammatical-feature Q110786    # singular\n  form L5785-F2                    # plural form\n    representation en surface-references\n    grammatical-feature Q146786    # plural\n  sense L5785-S1                   # gloss decomposed into word-lexeme ids, no quotes\n    gloss-source en (L3744 L3743)  # \"relationship\" \"relation\" (real lexeme ids)\n\nsurface-reference                  # the characters of \"reference\", by unicode code point\n  114 101 102 101 114 101 110 99 101   # r e f e r e n c e\nsurface-references\n  114 101 102 101 114 101 110 99 101 115   # r e f e r e n c e s\n```\n\nReal ids used above (verified): `L3744` = lexeme \"relationship\", `L3743` = lexeme \"relation\", `L3412` = \"between\", `L5848` = \"objects\". So the cached gloss is an **ordered link of lexeme ids**, not a quoted sentence — and it can itself be followed down to fully-formalized definitions. Nothing is a `\"...\"` blob.\n\nWhere a source string cannot yet be resolved to lexeme ids, store it as `unformalized-raw` with its characters as code points (still no quotes) and let a test flag it for later formalization — never leave it as a quoted reference.\n\n## Our formal definition references the cached ids (no English payload)\n\nOur semantic root stays pure colon-definitions; it **grounds** each concept in the real source id, and attaches surfaces as proper lexeme/sense links — not words:\n\n```lino\nreference: reference-action link          # definition: reference is a reference-action over a link\n  grounded-in Q121769                     # fact: grounded in the real wikidata concept\n  surface L5785-S4                        # fact: english noun sense that denotes this\n  surface L166084                         # fact: russian lexeme that denotes this\n```\n\nThis is parser-verified against the real `links-notation` Rust parser (`parse_lino`). The indented facts attach to the link whose head is `(reference: reference-action link)` — which is simply `reference` carrying its definition inline. So each fact reads exactly as `(reference grounded-in Q121769)`, `(reference surface L5785-S4)`, `(reference surface L166084)`: the subject **is** `reference`, and the colon part is just the embedded definition of that same reference. This is the preferred form — each fact's subject carries its own definition with it, explicitly.\n\nThe English/Russian *reading* of `reference` is then **generated** by translating the definition into the target language using the cached lexeme/form data — never stored as a description.\n\n## What to do — exactly\n\n1. **Write a migration script (Rust, re-runnable)** that converts the existing seed into the new format. No hand-authoring. It is also the converter for old snapshots.\n2. **Write a JSON→lino converter (Rust)** that does lossless true conversion of Wikidata/Wiktionary/Wikipedia responses, with a round-trip test (`json → lino → json` equals original). Precache the entities we actually reference (`Q121769`, `L5785`, `L41576`, `L166084`, `Q1084`, `Q1860`, `Q110786`, `Q146786`, …) under `data/cache/<source>/<id>.lino`.\n3. **Drop `meaning`, `gloss`, `description`, `lexeme \"xx\"/word` keys.** Facts are recorded by indentation under an id. Surfaces are lexeme/form/sense ids. Source strings live only in cache files, marked as source values.\n4. **Ground every concept in a real source id** (`grounded-in Q…`). No by-word source references.\n5. **Every id line gets a human-readable `# comment`.**\n6. **Minimal seed, expand on demand.** Seed ships only the core roots + the few cached entities needed to bootstrap. The system fetches and converts more (into lino cache) **on demand**, only as much as a given question/task needs. Do not try to memoize all of Wikidata.\n7. **Prove it with failing tests.** Add audits that fail if: any line **contains a quoted string `\"...\"`** (the single most important gate — quoted text is the fake); any seed line uses `gloss`/`description`/`meaning`/`word` keys; any source reference is a word rather than a `Q…`/`L…` id; the json→lino round-trip loses data. Words can be reinterpreted; a failing test cannot.\n\n## Suggested algorithm for the migration\n\n```\nfor each old `meaning \"<slug>\"` block:\n  mint formal id = the slug as a global reference symbol\n  emit colon-definition from defined_by/role, in the proposed format\n  for each old lexeme/word/description string:\n     resolve the surface to a real Wikidata lexeme id (L…) + sense (…-S…) via API\n     precache that lexeme's JSON, CONVERTED to lino (lossless, zero quotes:\n       surfaces -> character code points, glosses -> ordered lexeme ids)\n       under data/cache/wikidata/<id>.lino\n     attach `grounded-in Q…` and `surface L…-S…` to the formal definition\n     DELETE the english description string (regenerable by translation)\n  if a string cannot be resolved to ids -> store as unformalized-raw (code points,\n     no quotes) and flag via test; do NOT keep it as a quoted reference\nassert: NO quoted string anywhere; no gloss/description/meaning/word key;\n        every surface is an id; every source ref is a Q…/L… id; round-trip holds\n```\n\n## Definition of done\n\n- Migration script + json→lino converter exist; both have tests.\n- **`grep -rE '\"' data/seed/ data/cache/` returns NOTHING** — no quoted strings anywhere, enforced by a test. This is the primary gate.\n- `grep -rE '(gloss|description|meaning |word ) ' data/seed/` returns nothing, enforced by a test.\n- Every concept is `grounded-in` a real `Q…` id; every surface is an `L…`/sense id; every text is decomposed into character code points or lexeme ids; no bare-word source refs.\n- `data/cache/<source>/<id>.lino` files exist for every referenced id, lossless (round-trip test passes), zero quotes.\n- Descriptions are generated by translating formal definitions, not stored.\n- Seed is minimal; on-demand fetch+convert path works.\n- No parallel old+new structure remains.\n\nDo not mark \"ready to merge\" until all of the above pass. If anything is unclear, ask before implementing — do not substitute your own design.\n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/formal-ai/issues/comments/4640905488/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/formal-ai/issues/comments/4640910041","html_url":"https://github.com/link-assistant/formal-ai/pull/399#issuecomment-4640910041","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/formal-ai/issues/399","id":4640910041,"node_id":"IC_kwDOSbOoU88AAAABFJ6q2Q","user":{"login":"konard","id":1431904,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzE5MDQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1431904?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard","html_url":"https://github.com/konard","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-06-07T00:33:41Z","updated_at":"2026-06-07T00:33:41Z","body":"🤖 **AI Work Session Started**\n\nStarting automated work session at 2026-06-07T00:33:39.664Z\n\nThe PR has been converted to draft mode while work is in progress.\n\n_This comment marks the beginning of an AI work session. Please wait for the session to finish, and provide your feedback._","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/formal-ai/issues/comments/4640910041/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null}]
